/*  A method stores its argument in the object it was called on.
    Obligation broken: O4, what a function stores into its parameters is its caller's business. See docs/SOUNDNESS.md.  */

Define object bag with (the series of series of number items).
Bind void to keep unto bag, given (the series of number s):
    Insert s into one's items.
Done.
Define b as a new bag { the items (a series of series of number) }.
Pull a rabbit.
    Define inner as a series of number with (1, 2, 3).
    Cast b's keep on (inner).
Done.

/*  Make and drop enough values that freed memory is handed out again. */
Define churn as a series of text.
Define tick as 0.
While tick is less than 400, repeat:
    Insert ("zzzzzzzz" joined to "yyyyyyyy") into churn.
    tick becomes tick + 1.
Done.
State b's items.
